#
# holt — Groovy for a ctags that does not have it.
#
# Loaded ONLY after holt has MEASURED that this toolchain cannot extract Groovy symbols, and
# defined under a PRIVATE name. Both matter, and the reason is not hypothetical: this definition
# used to live in the always-loaded pack under the real name `Groovy`, and the moment upstream
# ctags gained its own Groovy parser the load became FATAL — "Language \"Groovy\" already
# defined", ctags exits, and holt gets ZERO symbols from EVERY file in the repository. Silence,
# which reads as "these agents share nothing".
#
# A private name cannot collide with a builtin. The measurement gate means a real builtin parser
# is never replaced by these regexes when one exists.
#
### Groovy #####################################################################
--langdef=HoltGroovy
--map-HoltGroovy=+.groovy
--map-HoltGroovy=+.gradle
--kinddef-HoltGroovy=f,function,methods
--kinddef-HoltGroovy=c,class,classes
--kinddef-HoltGroovy=v,variable,variables
--regex-HoltGroovy=/^[ \t]*(public|private|protected|static|final|abstract|[ \t])*(class|interface|trait|enum)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)/\3/c/
--regex-HoltGroovy=/^[ \t]*(public|private|protected|static|final|synchronized|def|[ \t])+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)[ \t]*\(/\2/f/
--regex-HoltGroovy=/^[ \t]*(def|final)[ \t]+([a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*)[ \t]*=/\2/v/
